          "filename": "Union Station (7168298597).jpg",
          "caption": "Union Station in Springfield (1898). It was built in 1898 by Illinois Central in response to the construction of a new Chicago and Alton Railroad station nearby. In 1900, passenger rail service began from Springfield to St. Louis, allowing a trip from Chicago to St. Louis with only one stop in Springfield. The Green Diamond, the first diesel electric locomotive, stopped here in 1936 on its inaugural journey en route to Chicago.",
